1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,050
Fifty-three point seven cents.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:05,610
That's how much tax you pay on every
single litre of petrol or diesel in

3
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:06,990
Australia right now.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,070
Fill up a big ute,

5
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,970
and you've handed the government around
forty dollars before you've even left

6
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:12,070
the servo.

7
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:16,190
Now imagine paying that and a new tax
for every kilometre you drive on top of

8
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:16,630
it.

9
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:18,590
That's not a conspiracy theory.

10
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,450
In October 2026,

11
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,250
Tesla the world's best-known electric
car company told a federal parliamentary

12
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,890
inquiry that petrol,

13
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,090
diesel and hybrid drivers should
pay a per-kilometre road charge,

14
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:30,610
while keeping fuel excise.

15
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:34,930
The Australian Electric Vehicle
Association has proposed something similar.

16
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:38,590
Polestar's Australian boss says a
road-user charge is "inevitable".

17
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,150
And New South Wales already has a law
for a per-kilometre charge on electric

18
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,370
cars, due to start in July 2027.

19
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:46,250
So in this video,

20
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,430
I'll explain exactly
what's being proposed,

21
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:49,310
who wants it,

22
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:51,890
what it could cost you
whether you drive a Corolla,

23
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,010
a LandCruiser or a Tesla and what
you can actually do about it.

24
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:58,610
Because the way Australians pay
for roads is about to change,

25
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:00,940
and it's going to affect
every driver in the country.

26
00:01:01,526 --> 00:01:03,236
To understand why this is happening,

27
00:01:03,286 --> 00:01:05,756
you need to understand how
roads are paid for today.

28
00:01:05,806 --> 00:01:10,176
Every time you buy fuel, you pay
fuel excise a fixed tax per litre.

29
00:01:10,226 --> 00:01:15,536
It went back up to around 53.7 cents
a litre on the 3rd of August 2026,

30
00:01:15,586 --> 00:01:18,516
after a temporary cut during
the fuel crisis ended.

31
00:01:18,566 --> 00:01:21,296
Before the cut, it was 52.6 cents.

32
00:01:21,346 --> 00:01:23,736
And it rises twice a year with inflation.

33
00:01:23,786 --> 00:01:25,876
During the 2026 fuel crisis,

34
00:01:25,926 --> 00:01:27,976
the government cut
excise for three months,

35
00:01:28,026 --> 00:01:30,056
then extended a smaller
cut for another month,

36
00:01:30,106 --> 00:01:32,776
before restoring the full rate in August.

37
00:01:32,826 --> 00:01:36,316
That cut alone showed how much money is
at stake and how politically sensitive

38
00:01:36,366 --> 00:01:37,856
fuel taxes are.

39
00:01:37,906 --> 00:01:41,836
It's also worth knowing that fuel
excise isn't a dedicated road fund.

40
00:01:41,886 --> 00:01:46,356
It goes into general government
revenue, alongside income tax and GST.

41
00:01:46,406 --> 00:01:48,356
Road funding comes out of that bigger pot,

42
00:01:48,406 --> 00:01:50,796
from federal, state and local governments.

43
00:01:50,846 --> 00:01:53,716
So when people say "EV
drivers don't pay for roads",

44
00:01:53,766 --> 00:01:57,276
it's a bit more complicated than that
but they're right that EV drivers don't

45
00:01:57,326 --> 00:01:58,826
pay the biggest motoring tax.

46
00:01:58,876 --> 00:02:02,676
Fuel excise raises roughly fifteen
billion dollars a year for the federal

47
00:02:02,726 --> 00:02:03,676
government.

48
00:02:03,726 --> 00:02:04,596
According to the ABC,

49
00:02:04,646 --> 00:02:10,196
the average petrol or diesel driver
pays about $1,400 a year in excise.

50
00:02:10,246 --> 00:02:11,146
But here's the problem.

51
00:02:11,196 --> 00:02:13,056
Electric cars don't use fuel.

52
00:02:13,106 --> 00:02:15,816
So EV drivers pay no fuel excise at all.

53
00:02:15,866 --> 00:02:17,876
And EVs are no longer a niche.

54
00:02:17,926 --> 00:02:19,756
In September 2026,

55
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:24,336
electric cars made up 24.2 per cent
of all new-vehicle sales in Australia,

56
00:02:24,386 --> 00:02:25,836
more than petrol cars.

57
00:02:25,886 --> 00:02:29,416
The Tesla Model Y beat the Ford Ranger
to become the country's best-selling

58
00:02:29,466 --> 00:02:33,516
vehicle in May 2026, and did
it again in June and August.

59
00:02:33,566 --> 00:02:36,066
As more people switch,
the excise money shrinks.

60
00:02:36,116 --> 00:02:39,436
Plug-in hybrids and efficient
hybrids burn less fuel too,

61
00:02:39,486 --> 00:02:41,076
so they pay less as well.

62
00:02:41,126 --> 00:02:43,883
The CEO of the advocacy
group Transport Australia,

63
00:02:43,933 --> 00:02:46,176
Ehssan Veiszadeh, summed it up:

64
00:02:46,226 --> 00:02:49,356
"Fuel excise was designed for a
different vehicle fleet and a different

65
00:02:49,406 --> 00:02:52,016
economy." So governments are
looking for a replacement.

66
00:02:52,066 --> 00:02:55,156
And the leading idea
is a road-user charge:

67
00:02:55,206 --> 00:02:57,616
a fee for every kilometre you drive.

68
00:02:57,666 --> 00:02:59,836
Australia wouldn't be
the first to do this.

69
00:02:59,886 --> 00:03:00,856
Across the Tasman,

70
00:03:00,906 --> 00:03:04,536
New Zealand made electric cars pay
road-user charges from the 1st of April

71
00:03:04,586 --> 00:03:09,716
2024: 76 New Zealand dollars per
thousand kilometres for a pure EV,

72
00:03:09,766 --> 00:03:14,496
and 53 dollars for a plug-in hybrid,
which still pays fuel tax at the pump.

73
00:03:14,546 --> 00:03:18,556
New Zealand's Automobile Association
estimated that an average driver covering

74
00:03:18,606 --> 00:03:23,296
12,000 kilometres a year
would pay about $912 in an EV.

75
00:03:23,346 --> 00:03:24,696
And in the United Kingdom,

76
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:28,956
the government announced in
late 2025 that from April 2028,

77
00:03:29,006 --> 00:03:30,896
electric cars will pay
three pence per mile,

78
00:03:30,946 --> 00:03:35,576
and plug-in hybrids one and a half
pence on top of existing vehicle tax.

79
00:03:35,626 --> 00:03:37,796
Drivers will estimate
their mileage each year,

80
00:03:37,846 --> 00:03:40,476
and it'll be checked at
the annual roadworthy test.

81
00:03:40,526 --> 00:03:42,456
So the direction around
the world is clear:

82
00:03:42,506 --> 00:03:45,366
if you don't pay at the pump,
you'll pay by the kilometre.

83
00:03:46,054 --> 00:03:49,124
The first state to try it
for real is New South Wales.

84
00:03:49,174 --> 00:03:52,464
NSW already has a road-user
charge written into law.

85
00:03:52,514 --> 00:03:55,404
For the 2026-27 financial year,

86
00:03:55,454 --> 00:04:00,424
the rate is 3.095 cents per kilometre
for battery-electric and hydrogen cars,

87
00:04:00,474 --> 00:04:05,184
and 2.476 cents for plug-in hybrids
that's eighty per cent of the full rate.

88
00:04:05,234 --> 00:04:07,824
The rate is indexed to
inflation every year.

89
00:04:07,874 --> 00:04:10,844
It's due to start on the 1st of July 2027,

90
00:04:10,894 --> 00:04:14,324
or when electric vehicles reach thirty
per cent of new-car sales whichever

91
00:04:14,374 --> 00:04:15,344
comes first.

92
00:04:15,394 --> 00:04:17,564
And that trigger is closer
than you might think.

93
00:04:17,614 --> 00:04:19,824
In the June 2026 quarter,

94
00:04:19,874 --> 00:04:23,264
battery EVs made up about 21
per cent of national sales.

95
00:04:23,314 --> 00:04:26,664
Add plug-in hybrids, and it
was around 31.6 per cent.

96
00:04:26,714 --> 00:04:29,924
It's not yet clear exactly how
the trigger will be measured.

97
00:04:29,974 --> 00:04:31,224
What would it cost?

98
00:04:31,274 --> 00:04:35,404
Drive 15,000 kilometres a year in
an electric car in New South Wales,

99
00:04:35,454 --> 00:04:39,244
and at today's rate,
that's about $464 a year.

100
00:04:39,294 --> 00:04:40,484
But there's a big legal problem.

101
00:04:40,534 --> 00:04:41,984
In October 2023,

102
00:04:42,034 --> 00:04:46,144
the High Court ruled four to three that
Victoria's distance-based charge on

103
00:04:46,194 --> 00:04:49,884
electric cars was a duty of
excise and under the Constitution,

104
00:04:49,934 --> 00:04:52,304
only the federal government
can impose excise.

105
00:04:52,354 --> 00:04:54,324
The Victorian scheme was struck down.

106
00:04:54,374 --> 00:04:56,334
The NSW scheme has a similar structure,

107
00:04:56,384 --> 00:04:59,864
and NSW says it's still
assessing the implications.

108
00:04:59,914 --> 00:05:01,724
As of September 2026,

109
00:05:01,774 --> 00:05:05,364
no EV road-user charge was actually
being collected anywhere in Australia.

110
00:05:05,414 --> 00:05:09,484
Western Australia had also
announced a planned charge for 2027,

111
00:05:09,534 --> 00:05:14,284
of 2.5 cents per kilometre for battery
EVs and 2 cents for plug-in hybrids,

112
00:05:14,334 --> 00:05:16,284
alongside an EV rebate.

113
00:05:16,334 --> 00:05:18,614
Whether those rates
still stand is unclear.

114
00:05:19,441 --> 00:05:22,821
Because of that High Court ruling,
the real decision sits in Canberra.

115
00:05:22,871 --> 00:05:26,911
Treasurer Jim Chalmers has called a
road-user charge "an idea whose time has

116
00:05:26,961 --> 00:05:30,871
come," and federal and state treasurers
have agreed reform is needed.

117
00:05:30,921 --> 00:05:32,711
But in August 2025,

118
00:05:32,761 --> 00:05:34,851
Chalmers said the focus would
be on electric vehicles,

119
00:05:34,901 --> 00:05:39,211
and that the government wasn't trying
to "double-tax" petrol and diesel cars.

120
00:05:39,261 --> 00:05:40,771
Then things slowed down.

121
00:05:40,821 --> 00:05:44,611
The May 2026 federal budget
did not introduce a charge.

122
00:05:44,661 --> 00:05:46,211
The government said it "needs more work".

123
00:05:46,261 --> 00:05:49,001
Climate Change and Energy
Minister Chris Bowen said:

124
00:05:49,051 --> 00:05:52,231
"I think a road-user charge is something
that Australia should be working

125
00:05:52,281 --> 00:05:54,931
towards," but added: "It's
got to be done right.

126
00:05:54,981 --> 00:05:56,331
It's got to be done carefully,

127
00:05:56,381 --> 00:06:00,911
and that includes timing." CarExpert
reported that a 2028 start had been

128
00:06:00,961 --> 00:06:05,091
planned, but that the announcement was
postponed amid record fuel prices and

129
00:06:05,141 --> 00:06:06,471
rising EV sales.

130
00:06:06,521 --> 00:06:09,911
Transport Minister Catherine King has
said the government doesn't want to

131
00:06:09,961 --> 00:06:12,431
discourage people from
buying electric cars.

132
00:06:12,481 --> 00:06:15,471
The Greens oppose any charge
that targets EV drivers.

133
00:06:15,521 --> 00:06:17,931
And the Australian Automobile Association,

134
00:06:17,981 --> 00:06:19,971
which represents the state motoring clubs,

135
00:06:20,021 --> 00:06:23,531
wants a charge legislated
in the 2027 budget.

136
00:06:23,581 --> 00:06:25,431
So the federal position, for now, is:

137
00:06:25,481 --> 00:06:27,011
a charge is coming eventually,

138
00:06:27,061 --> 00:06:30,191
it would mainly target EVs,
and nobody is promising when.

139
00:06:30,241 --> 00:06:34,531
And remember, the government is also
changing EV incentives at the same time.

140
00:06:34,581 --> 00:06:39,151
It extended the Electric Car Discount
on novated leases to April 2027,

141
00:06:39,201 --> 00:06:43,111
after which the full discount will
be limited to vehicles priced under

142
00:06:43,161 --> 00:06:44,171
$75,000.

143
00:06:44,221 --> 00:06:47,631
Put a smaller tax break and a new
per-kilometre charge together,

144
00:06:47,681 --> 00:06:52,711
and the cost of owning an EV in 2027
and 2028 could look quite different from

145
00:06:52,761 --> 00:06:53,561
today.

146
00:06:54,114 --> 00:06:58,324
And that's where Tesla comes in
with a twist almost nobody expected.

147
00:06:58,374 --> 00:07:01,064
In a submission to a federal
parliamentary inquiry,

148
00:07:01,114 --> 00:07:03,374
the Select Committee on
Productivity in Australia,

149
00:07:03,424 --> 00:07:07,644
Tesla Australia argued that a road-user
charge should not apply only to

150
00:07:07,694 --> 00:07:08,904
electric cars.

151
00:07:08,954 --> 00:07:13,024
It said the charge should "apply it
universally to all vehicles on the road,

152
00:07:13,074 --> 00:07:16,784
phased-in," with the rate based
on "real road funding costs".

153
00:07:16,834 --> 00:07:18,604
Here's the controversial part.

154
00:07:18,654 --> 00:07:20,824
Tesla proposed keeping
fuel excise as well.

155
00:07:20,874 --> 00:07:23,604
That means drivers of
newly registered petrol,

156
00:07:23,654 --> 00:07:26,524
diesel and hybrid vehicles
would eventually pay both:

157
00:07:26,574 --> 00:07:29,984
the excise on their fuel, and
a charge for every kilometre.

158
00:07:30,034 --> 00:07:31,644
Why would Tesla want that?

159
00:07:31,694 --> 00:07:35,624
Its argument is that an EV-only charge
"acts as a financial penalty for

160
00:07:35,674 --> 00:07:37,724
decarbonising personal transport".

161
00:07:37,774 --> 00:07:41,244
It said a charge on EVs alone would
"distort" what people think motoring

162
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,204
costs.

163
00:07:42,254 --> 00:07:44,844
And it argued that fuel excise
doesn't really change behaviour,

164
00:07:44,894 --> 00:07:48,864
because "consumers remain largely
inelastic to the tax component of their

165
00:07:48,914 --> 00:07:52,244
travel", while a per-kilometre
charge would encourage people to skip

166
00:07:52,294 --> 00:07:55,824
unnecessary trips and use
public or active transport.

167
00:07:55,874 --> 00:07:58,504
Of course, Tesla sells only electric cars.

168
00:07:58,554 --> 00:08:00,684
A system that taxes its customers less,

169
00:08:00,734 --> 00:08:03,384
and everyone else more,
would suit its business.

170
00:08:03,434 --> 00:08:07,034
That doesn't make the argument wrong
but it's worth knowing who's making it.

171
00:08:07,727 --> 00:08:10,737
Quick favour before we get to the numbers
because this is where it could hit

172
00:08:10,787 --> 00:08:11,757
your wallet.

173
00:08:11,807 --> 00:08:14,637
Do you think every driver should
pay a per-kilometre charge,

174
00:08:14,687 --> 00:08:17,017
or only EV owners, or nobody at all?

175
00:08:17,067 --> 00:08:19,837
Tell me in the comments I
want to hear both sides.

176
00:08:19,887 --> 00:08:22,677
And if you want straight-talking
videos about what's changing for Aussie

177
00:08:22,727 --> 00:08:24,337
drivers, hit subscribe.

178
00:08:24,387 --> 00:08:26,507
It's free and it really helps the channel.

179
00:08:27,321 --> 00:08:30,691
Tesla isn't the only one pushing
for a charge on everyone.

180
00:08:30,741 --> 00:08:32,621
On the 17th of September 2026,

181
00:08:32,671 --> 00:08:36,751
the Australian Electric Vehicle
Association a volunteer-run,

182
00:08:36,801 --> 00:08:39,631
not-for-profit group
released its own proposal.

183
00:08:39,681 --> 00:08:42,291
Electric cars would
pay a road-user charge.

184
00:08:42,341 --> 00:08:44,591
Petrol and diesel vehicles
would pay the same charge,

185
00:08:44,641 --> 00:08:46,691
plus the existing fuel excise,

186
00:08:46,741 --> 00:08:49,861
which the association calls a
"highly efficient pollution tax".

187
00:08:49,911 --> 00:08:52,751
Its version is based
on weight and distance.

188
00:08:52,801 --> 00:08:56,271
The rate would phase in over ten years
to three cents per tonne-kilometre.

189
00:08:56,321 --> 00:08:58,131
The association's own example:

190
00:08:58,181 --> 00:09:03,711
a 2.2-tonne diesel ute or electric SUV
driven 13,000 kilometres a year would

191
00:09:03,761 --> 00:09:05,841
pay $858 annually.

192
00:09:05,891 --> 00:09:09,521
Odometer readings would be taken
every six or twelve months.

193
00:09:09,571 --> 00:09:14,311
AEVA policy convenor Dr Chris Jones said
that for vehicles of equal weight and

194
00:09:14,361 --> 00:09:17,971
distance, "it's only fair that
they pay the same road user charge.

195
00:09:18,021 --> 00:09:20,631
But if one of those vehicles
burns petrol or diesel,

196
00:09:20,681 --> 00:09:23,373
they should pay for the cost of
that pollution too." He added:

197
00:09:23,423 --> 00:09:24,467
"We're not after a free ride,

198
00:09:24,517 --> 00:09:26,591
but we are asking for policy which
encourages EV adoption." Polestar agrees

199
00:09:26,641 --> 00:09:30,511
with the principle.

200
00:09:30,561 --> 00:09:33,991
In October 2026, Polestar
Australia's managing director,

201
00:09:34,041 --> 00:09:38,271
Scott Maynard, told CarExpert he sees
"the inevitable introduction of a

202
00:09:38,321 --> 00:09:42,491
road-user charge", and that it should
apply to all motorists, based on weight.

203
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:42,987
He pointed out:

204
00:09:43,037 --> 00:09:47,071
"We don't have a congestion tax in
Australia." And it's not just electric car

205
00:09:47,121 --> 00:09:47,891
companies.

206
00:09:47,941 --> 00:09:50,351
The Australian Automotive
Dealer Association,

207
00:09:50,401 --> 00:09:51,671
led by James Voortman,

208
00:09:51,721 --> 00:09:55,131
has called for a national road-user
charge for all vehicle types,

209
00:09:55,181 --> 00:09:57,571
as part of a full review of vehicle taxes.

210
00:09:57,621 --> 00:10:01,651
The Australian Automobile Association
has called for a distance-based charge,

211
00:10:01,701 --> 00:10:04,761
developed with the states
and modelled on the NSW plan.

212
00:10:05,559 --> 00:10:08,729
There's also a version that tries
to protect working families.

213
00:10:08,779 --> 00:10:10,349
In May 2026,

214
00:10:10,399 --> 00:10:13,589
the McKell Institute released
a study called Fairer Roads,

215
00:10:13,639 --> 00:10:15,809
backed by the Electric Vehicle Council.

216
00:10:15,859 --> 00:10:19,853
It proposed introducing a road-user
charge once electric cars reach thirty per

217
00:10:19,903 --> 00:10:23,349
cent of Australia's whole
fleet not just new sales.

218
00:10:23,399 --> 00:10:24,589
Rates would be set by income,

219
00:10:24,639 --> 00:10:29,869
across four levels from 3.74
to 12.86 cents per kilometre.

220
00:10:29,919 --> 00:10:33,149
Once electric vehicles passed
seventy-five per cent of the fleet,

221
00:10:33,199 --> 00:10:36,809
the charge would apply to all
vehicles and replace fuel excise.

222
00:10:36,859 --> 00:10:37,559
In the meantime,

223
00:10:37,609 --> 00:10:41,469
fuel-powered cars would pay an extra
carbon surcharge of half a cent to one

224
00:10:41,519 --> 00:10:43,249
and a half cents per kilometre.

225
00:10:43,299 --> 00:10:45,749
McKell's chief executive,
Edward Cavanough,

226
00:10:45,799 --> 00:10:49,129
argued that families in the outer
suburbs drive the furthest and have the

227
00:10:49,179 --> 00:10:53,349
fewest alternatives, so a flat
per-kilometre charge would hit them hardest.

228
00:10:53,399 --> 00:10:56,649
And interestingly, a lot
of EV owners don't object.

229
00:10:56,699 --> 00:11:00,749
Research released by Transport Australia
found 71 per cent of electric and

230
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:04,929
hybrid drivers support a road-user
charge the highest support of any group

231
00:11:04,979 --> 00:11:05,949
surveyed.

232
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:08,729
The debate isn't really
about whether EVs should pay.

233
00:11:08,779 --> 00:11:11,179
It's about whether everyone
else should pay more too.

234
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:13,570
So what could this actually cost you?

235
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:14,590
Let me be clear:

236
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:17,330
these are illustrations based
on the published proposals,

237
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:18,890
not confirmed prices.

238
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:21,290
None of them is law at
the federal level yet.

239
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:25,550
Say you drive an electric car 15,000
kilometres a year in New South Wales.

240
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:32,050
At the legislated NSW rate of 3.095
cents, that's about $464 a year.

241
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:35,290
Now say the charge was set at the level
that would roughly match what a petrol

242
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:36,890
car pays in excise.

243
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:40,550
Secondary reporting of a Parliamentary
Budget Office costing puts that at

244
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,030
about 5.3 cents per kilometre.

245
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:47,710
Over 15,000 kilometres,
that's around $795 a year.

246
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,630
Under the electric vehicle
association's weight-based plan,

247
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:57,250
that 2.2-tonne ute or SUV doing 13,000
kilometres would pay $858 a year.

248
00:11:57,300 --> 00:12:00,490
If it's a diesel ute, that
comes on top of fuel excise.

249
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:05,230
A ute using around nine litres per
hundred kilometres would burn about 1,170

250
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:10,990
litres over that distance roughly
$628 in excise at today's rate.

251
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:14,610
Together, that's nearly fifteen hundred
dollars a year in road taxes for one

252
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:15,490
vehicle.

253
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:18,450
And under Tesla's proposal,
newly registered petrol,

254
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:22,930
diesel and hybrid cars would also pay
both the exact rate would depend on what

255
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:25,370
governments decided the
real cost of roads is.

256
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:28,730
That's why this matters to every
driver, not just EV owners.

257
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:31,870
The difference between the proposals
is the difference between a few hundred

258
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,100
dollars a year and well over a thousand.

259
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:35,926
So who's right?

260
00:12:35,976 --> 00:12:38,226
Here are the strongest
arguments on both sides.

261
00:12:38,276 --> 00:12:41,646
Supporters say a road-user
charge is simply fairer.

262
00:12:41,696 --> 00:12:44,966
Everyone uses the roads, so
everyone should pay for them.

263
00:12:45,016 --> 00:12:49,086
Heavier vehicles cause more wear,
so weight-based charges make sense.

264
00:12:49,136 --> 00:12:51,386
And without reform, the money for roads,

265
00:12:51,436 --> 00:12:54,816
potholes and highways will keep
shrinking as the fleet goes electric.

266
00:12:54,866 --> 00:12:58,746
Critics say a charge on top of
fuel excise is a double tax,

267
00:12:58,796 --> 00:13:02,086
at a time when Australians are already
struggling with the cost of living and

268
00:13:02,136 --> 00:13:02,986
record fuel prices.

269
00:13:03,036 --> 00:13:05,386
Regional and outer-suburban drivers,

270
00:13:05,436 --> 00:13:08,606
who travel the longest distances
and have no public transport,

271
00:13:08,656 --> 00:13:10,346
would pay the most.

272
00:13:10,396 --> 00:13:11,706
Some worry about privacy,

273
00:13:11,756 --> 00:13:15,526
if kilometres are tracked by GPS
rather than odometer readings.

274
00:13:15,576 --> 00:13:19,286
EV advocates warn that charging electric
cars too early could slow the switch

275
00:13:19,336 --> 00:13:21,006
away from petrol and diesel.

276
00:13:21,056 --> 00:13:25,186
And the High Court ruling means any state
scheme could face a legal challenge.

277
00:13:25,236 --> 00:13:27,846
There's also the question of
how the money is collected.

278
00:13:27,896 --> 00:13:31,226
The simplest approach is odometer
readings at rego renewal,

279
00:13:31,276 --> 00:13:33,566
at a service, or when a car is sold.

280
00:13:33,616 --> 00:13:36,186
That's what New Zealand
and the UK rely on.

281
00:13:36,236 --> 00:13:40,066
GPS tracking can be more precise and
could allow peak-hour or city-based

282
00:13:40,116 --> 00:13:43,326
pricing, but it raises
bigger privacy concerns.

283
00:13:43,376 --> 00:13:47,006
And any system has to stop people
winding back odometers or under-reporting

284
00:13:47,056 --> 00:13:48,246
their distance.

285
00:13:48,296 --> 00:13:50,166
Both sides agree on one thing:

286
00:13:50,216 --> 00:13:53,006
fuel excise alone won't pay
for Australia's roads forever.

287
00:13:53,056 --> 00:13:56,616
The fight is over who
pays, how much, and when.

288
00:13:57,406 --> 00:13:59,096
So what should you do right now?

289
00:13:59,146 --> 00:14:00,616
First, don't panic.

290
00:14:00,666 --> 00:14:02,596
As of September 2026,

291
00:14:02,646 --> 00:14:05,276
no road-user charge was being
collected anywhere in Australia,

292
00:14:05,326 --> 00:14:08,576
and the federal government
has not legislated one.

293
00:14:08,626 --> 00:14:12,116
Second, if you're buying an electric
car or a plug-in hybrid in New South

294
00:14:12,166 --> 00:14:16,116
Wales, factor in a possible
charge from July 2027.

295
00:14:16,166 --> 00:14:18,016
At around three cents per kilometre,

296
00:14:18,066 --> 00:14:21,836
budget roughly four to five hundred
dollars a year for typical driving.

297
00:14:21,886 --> 00:14:25,116
It still usually works out cheaper
than fuel but it's not nothing.

298
00:14:25,166 --> 00:14:29,096
Third, keep good records of your
odometer readings and servicing.

299
00:14:29,146 --> 00:14:31,276
Every proposal so far relies on distance,

300
00:14:31,326 --> 00:14:34,876
and accurate records protect
you if you're ever charged.

301
00:14:34,926 --> 00:14:36,406
And fourth, have your say.

302
00:14:36,456 --> 00:14:40,096
Federal inquiries and state
reviews take public submissions.

303
00:14:40,146 --> 00:14:41,816
Motoring clubs, dealer groups,

304
00:14:41,866 --> 00:14:44,936
EV groups and car companies
are all lobbying hard.

305
00:14:44,986 --> 00:14:46,736
Ordinary drivers should too.

306
00:14:46,786 --> 00:14:48,456
Here's the timeline to watch.

307
00:14:48,506 --> 00:14:51,736
NSW's charge is due from
the 1st of July 2027,

308
00:14:51,786 --> 00:14:55,116
unless it's delayed, changed
or challenged in court.

309
00:14:55,166 --> 00:14:58,916
The motoring clubs want a federal
charge legislated in the 2027 budget.

310
00:14:58,966 --> 00:15:03,556
And the next federal election will decide
which party gets to write the rules.

311
00:15:03,606 --> 00:15:06,976
So, could every Aussie driver
end up paying a new road tax?

312
00:15:07,026 --> 00:15:09,576
It's being seriously proposed by Tesla,

313
00:15:09,626 --> 00:15:13,336
by electric vehicle groups, by
car dealers and by motoring clubs.

314
00:15:13,386 --> 00:15:15,776
The federal government
says it's focused on EVs,

315
00:15:15,826 --> 00:15:17,596
and it isn't promising a date.

316
00:15:17,646 --> 00:15:20,376
But the old system is running out
of road, and change is coming.

317
00:15:20,426 --> 00:15:23,096
If this helped, hit like, subscribe,

318
00:15:23,146 --> 00:15:25,116
and share it with
someone who drives a lot.

319
00:15:25,166 --> 00:15:28,886
Tell me in the comments: should
everyone pay, only EVs, or nobody?

320
00:15:28,936 --> 00:15:30,726
And I'll see you in the next video.
